connection string
has two formats: STANDARD and SRV

STANDARD:
mongodb://username:password@host:port/database

SRV:
mongodb+srv://
Atlas deployments use srv format
By using srv, it indicates to mongosh that the host name that follows corresponds to a DNS SRV record.
No port needed, whereas in standard format, host:port format is used
Also by using SRV, it sets TLS to true and connect to the DNS seed list

default port for mdb is 27017
we can also use a different port
mongosh --port 27777
